Phase 3 — Stop hook (mechanical “DSA last”)

.cursor/hooks.json

{
  "version": 1,
  "hooks": {
    "stop": [
      {
        "command": ".cursor/hooks/stop_dsa_fitness.sh",
        "timeout": 120,
        "loop_limit": 8,
        "failClosed": false
      }
    ]
  }
}

Hook algorithm (stop_dsa_fitness.sh → Python helper)





Read stdin JSON: status, loop_count



If status == "aborted" → print {} and exit (do not fight the user)



If loop_count >= loop_limit → print {} and write harness/reports/loop_exhausted.md (human must intervene / /harness-steer)



Run python -m harness --mode agent



If overall pass → append knowledge success → print {}



If fail → build followup_message from remediation.py including:





Failed stage name (especially if DSA)



First 3 remediation bullets



Exact re-run command



Explicit: “Do not claim done. Fix, then re-run until DSA is green.”

This implements Osmani/Liran Tal back-pressure: agent stop → verify → auto continue until green or cap.

Optional later: afterFileEdit for cheap AST-only on *.py (keep quality left without full DSA every keystroke). Full DSA stays on stop only (cost).



